highlighted the contributions of ITBP towards internal security and border safeguarding. Meanwhile, the Indian Army and Home Minister Amit Shah also conveyed their regards.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/itbp-raising-day-pm-modi-praises-himveers-as-india-china-border-management-remains-in-focus/articleshow/135161153.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/itbp-raising-day-pm-modi-praises-himveers-as-india-china-border-management-remains-in-focus/articleshow/135161153.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T09:37:39+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135161465,imgsize-841057.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kerala governor Om Prakash Mathur's 'veg-only kitchen' diktat on first day of assuming office sparks row]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kerala-governor-om-prakash-mathurs-veg-only-kitchen-diktat-on-first-day-of-assuming-office-sparks-row/articleshow/135160310.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135160310.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kerala-governor-om-prakash-mathurs-veg-only-kitchen-diktat-on-first-day-of-assuming-office-sparks-row/articleshow/135160310.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kerala-governor-om-prakash-mathurs-veg-only-kitchen-diktat-on-first-day-of-assuming-office-sparks-row/articleshow/135160310.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T08:38:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135160777,imgsize-112250.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[India highlights nuclear advances, development partnerships at UNGA session]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-highlights-nuclear-advances-development-partnerships-at-unga-session/articleshow/135159961.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135159961.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[India has expressed its dedication to peaceful nuclear technology and support for the International Atomic Energy Agency. Several countries have acknowledged India's development assistance during the Ninth Annual India-UN Development Partnership Fund event. Ambassadors from various nations highlighted how India's support aligns with their national priorities and fosters South-South cooperation. IAEA's director-general projected significant growth in global nuclear power usage driven by technological demands.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-highlights-nuclear-advances-development-partnerships-at-unga-session/articleshow/135159961.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-highlights-nuclear-advances-development-partnerships-at-unga-session/articleshow/135159961.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T08:08:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135160254,imgsize-63426.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[After Operation Sindoor friction, Delhi &amp; Baku reset ties with EAM Jaishankar's visit]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/after-operation-sindoor-friction-delhi-baku-reset-ties-with-eam-jaishankars-visit/articleshow/135155334.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135155334.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Ties between the two countries had been held back by geopolitical reasons for a while, mainly Azerbaijan’s ties with Pakistan — as evident from its support for Islamabad after Op Sindoor last year — and India’s defence ties with Armenia. While Bayramov spoke about taking the relationship to a higher level, setting aside past differences, Jaishankar underlined the significance of trade and energy cooperation. Terrorism was also discussed.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/after-operation-sindoor-friction-delhi-baku-reset-ties-with-eam-jaishankars-visit/articleshow/135155334.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/after-operation-sindoor-friction-delhi-baku-reset-ties-with-eam-jaishankars-visit/articleshow/135155334.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T01:36:48+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135155369,imgsize-48706.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Study traces how an El Niño changed the pollution map]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/study-traces-how-an-el-nio-changed-the-pollution-map/articleshow/135154890.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135154890.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Coming ahead of India’s peak pollution season, the paper, titled ‘Air quality in flux: The baffling ENSO transition in India’, published in Atmospheric Pollution Research journal Thursday, found that La Niña/El Niño conditions altered atmospheric circulation, PM2.5 transport pathways and weather conditions that determine whether pollution disperses or gets trapped.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/study-traces-how-an-el-nio-changed-the-pollution-map/articleshow/135154890.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/study-traces-how-an-el-nio-changed-the-pollution-map/articleshow/135154890.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T01:32:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Amitava Bhattacharya</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135155262,imgsize-1950721.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Cabinet secretariat merely acknowledged complaint of ECs against senior poll officer: RTI]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cabinet-secretariat-merely-acknowledged-complaint-of-ecs-against-senior-poll-officer-rti/articleshow/135154891.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135154891.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Explaining the rationale behind the reluctance to take any action, a confidential note on the file shared by the Cabinet secretariat with transparency activist, Commodore Lokesh K Batra (Retd), as part of its 21-page RTI reply, stated that EC being a Constitutional body is insulated from the Executive's interference by design.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cabinet-secretariat-merely-acknowledged-complaint-of-ecs-against-senior-poll-officer-rti/articleshow/135154891.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cabinet-secretariat-merely-acknowledged-complaint-of-ecs-against-senior-poll-officer-rti/articleshow/135154891.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T01:28:41+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135155199,imgsize-309298.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[China’s patrolling deviations disturb border: MEA on ITBP DG's LAC face-offs remark]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/chinas-patrolling-deviations-disturb-border-mea-on-itbp-dgs-lac-face-offs-remark/articleshow/135155021.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135155021.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The ministry of external affairs (MEA) on Friday did not go into the specifics of the latest face-off, choosing to refer the issue to the defence ministry, but said Chinese divergence from established patrolling patterns created disturbances at the border from time to time. The official said both sides continued to use existing diplomatic and military mechanisms to resolve outstanding issues and avoid misunderstanding and miscalculation along the LAC.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/chinas-patrolling-deviations-disturb-border-mea-on-itbp-dgs-lac-face-offs-remark/articleshow/135155021.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/chinas-patrolling-deviations-disturb-border-mea-on-itbp-dgs-lac-face-offs-remark/articleshow/135155021.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T01:25:14+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135155098,imgsize-45698.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Northwest India turned drier, south wetter over 70 years, finds IMD study]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/northwest-india-turned-drier-south-wetter-over-70-years-finds-imd-study/articleshow/135154893.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135154893.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In northwest India, the hot semi-arid zone grew from about a quarter of the region’s area in 1951-1980 to a third in 1991-2020, while the temperate zone shrank from about a quarter to less than a fifth, meaning that an area equal to roughly 7% of the region moved into the drier zone as temperatures rose and rainfall declined, said the study.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/northwest-india-turned-drier-south-wetter-over-70-years-finds-imd-study/articleshow/135154893.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/northwest-india-turned-drier-south-wetter-over-70-years-finds-imd-study/articleshow/135154893.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T01:24:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vishwa Mohan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135155143,imgsize-294286.cms"/></item></channel></rss>